1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,250
What if you cut a magnet in half?

2
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:05,920
If you cut a bar magnet in half,
do you get one N piece and one S piece?

3
00:00:05,970 --> 00:00:08,240
Let's cut it!

4
00:00:08,290 --> 00:00:10,410
Each piece gets
its own N and S!

5
00:00:10,460 --> 00:00:12,730
What if we cut again?

6
00:00:12,780 --> 00:00:16,500
All four pieces have N and S!
There's no magnet with only N

7
00:00:16,550 --> 00:00:18,670
Inside a piece of iron
there are tiny little magnets

8
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:21,940
When those tiny magnets
all line up the same way = a magnet!

9
00:00:21,990 --> 00:00:24,360
Cut it in the middle,
and the lines stay the same

10
00:00:24,410 --> 00:00:28,130
So a new N and S appear
right where you cut

11
00:00:28,180 --> 00:00:30,320
What if you bring the two pieces close again?

12
00:00:30,370 --> 00:00:33,690
Snap! They become one again

13
00:00:33,740 --> 00:00:36,340
Don't cut a real magnet
(broken pieces can be sharp)

14
00:00:36,390 --> 00:00:39,040
See you in the next experiment!
